/Users/robin/Obsidian/Brain/Projects/Gold Rush/E1 landmark atlas hashes drifted during the owner file swap — 2026-07-18 0952.md:10:The accepted E1 landmark replacement at `d8603c90` changed the atlases and 25 GLBs for The Claim, Dry Gulch, Twin Banks, Night Shift, and Baron without refreshing the older pack contracts. The live atlas file and every embedded GLB texture agree; the contract and aggregate-evidence atlas hashes were stale and are corrected on `sol/lm-alpha-atlas-hash-drift`.
/Users/robin/Obsidian/Brain/Projects/Gold Rush/Buildings must show condition through construction not brown noise — 2026-07-14-075914.md:12:The condition must belong to the contract. The Claim can be maintained but visibly patched. Dry Gulch should have actual failure: a roof opening, shortened chimney, collapsed canopy, and fallen panel. Twin Banks and Night Shift need repaired work sheds rather than neutral boxes. The Baron needs impact repairs, missing wall teeth, and contact shadows.
/Users/robin/Obsidian/Brain/Projects/Gold Rush/Claim Line cannot create hero-only firing perches — 2026-07-13 1242.md:16:The current balance confirms the asymmetry. The Spark Rig has range 10 and can gain additional range from elevation; ordinary enemies deal contact damage and seek the hero on the traversable terrain graph. The Baron rocket volley is a special exception, not a general answer to unreachable perches.
/Users/robin/Obsidian/Brain/Projects/Gold Rush/Every Epoch 1 contract owns a unique terrain inside one regional grammar — 2026-07-14 0512.md:18:This supersedes the earlier recommendation that Night Shift and Baron should reuse The Claim terrain. They still share The Claim's runtime river and ford topology, because simulation remains planar and code-owned, but they now have separate render-only heightfields: Night Shift is a rock-bound seven-lantern work corridor; Baron is an occupied river fortress with far-bank hierarchy, trench, bastions, and siege dressing.
/Users/robin/Obsidian/Brain/Projects/Gold Rush/Fevered enemies reuse the watch-paint instanced channel — 2026-07-13 1338.md:10:The runtime Fever tell reuses `EnemyPool`'s existing four instanced watch-paint meshes, so it adds no mesh or draw-call family. Humans expose only the face fitting as a warm gold glint; `steam_wrecker` exposes the three upper fittings as machine rivets/gauges. Rest strength is `0.34` with a `±0.04` pulse; grabbing or swinging surges to `0.70` with `±0.08`. Baron and railcar are hard-excluded. The accent obeys the existing Night Shift visibility factor and normal depth testing, so it cannot reveal threats outside light coverage or through world occluders.
/Users/robin/Obsidian/Brain/Projects/Gold Rush/AP-16 final verbs preserve seeded hashes — 2026-08-12 1320 ICT.md:18:The class-8 audit moved 66 rows from `agent-lacks` to `equal`: overall `agent-lacks 439 -> 373`, `equal 641 -> 707`. Four cited exemptions remain: post-death action, between-run research choice, pause pacing, and `skip_ceremony`. Headless Baron spawn bypasses ceremony directly at `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts:486`.
