🟢 **F-1656-1 CURED s1657 `34613d84e` — AND THE DIAGNOSIS IN THE ROW BELOW IS WRONG IN THE WAY THAT DECIDES THE CURE. READ THIS FIRST.** F-1656-1 recorded that the runner’s auto-commit `git add` was **"rejected"** and **"aborted"**, so the commit never ran — and prescribed re-scoping the add to the master’s TOUCH-ONLY list, or retrying with the legitimate paths. 🔬 **REPRODUCED ON A SCRATCH REPO (s1657), WHICH IS WHAT THE ROW’S OWN GATE DEMANDED, AND THE ADD DOES NOT ABORT.** It stages every legitimate path, correctly withholds the ignored one, and **then exits 1 purely to ADVISE** that an ignored path matched its pathspec (*"The following paths are ignored… hint: Use -f"*). Measured, git 2.50.1: **ARM 1** `git add -A -- . ':(exclude).wrangler'` → **rc=1 with the real file STAGED** · **ARM 5** the runner’s exact `add && commit` → **work stranded in the index, HEAD unmoved** (F-1656-1 reproduced exactly) · **ARM 6** `add ; commit` → **commit rc=0, index clean, and the ignored path did NOT leak in**. ➡️ **So the pathspec was never the defect — the `&&` was.** It read an advisory exit code as a failure and threw away an add that had already succeeded. **The prescribed cure would have rewritten a working pathspec and left the real fault in place.** ✅ **THE FIX IS ONE SEPARATOR AT EACH OF THE TWO COMMIT SITES** (`;` not `&&`), applied to the lane branch **and** the art branch together, because a cure that reaches one leaves the sibling defective — the shape that cost F-1154-1 an extra incident. Decoupling is safe for a reason that was checked rather than assumed: `git commit -- <pathspec>` takes its content from the **working tree through its own pathspec** (what F-1154-1 bought), so the commit can publish nothing the add would have withheld — ARM 6 confirms the ignored path stays out. 🔒 **GUARDED: `scripts/runner-commit-decoupling-guard.test.sh`**, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`. It checks BEHAVIOUR before source text — manufacturing the ignored-path condition on a scratch repo and asserting the compound form strands the work while the decoupled form commits it — then asserts both sites are decoupled, that the debris excludes still hold, and **proves its own red path** by restoring the `&&` on a scratch copy of the runner and requiring rejection. 8/8 green. ⏳ **INERT UNTIL THE RUNNER RESTARTS, AND THAT IS NOT A QUIBBLE — IT IS THIS FIX’S ENTIRE RISK.** bash parses the `while true` loop (`:72–:348`) whole and never re-reads it, so pid 52675 (up since 10:11) keeps running the OLD logic and **can still strand a lane’s work on every task it completes**. s1436 measured seven consecutive runner cures sitting inert for 23 days for exactly this reason. Not restarted this fire **by choice**: lane-d was mid-run on `agent-reels-2` from 11:46, and killing a runner mid-task abandons the work the cure exists to protect. ➡️ **OWED, AND IT IS A FIRE’S JOB NOT THE OWNER’S (§2.0b):** the runner is detached (`PPID 1`, `TTY ??`) = a fire’s own. **The next fire that finds all four lanes idle: `kill -TERM 52675` (re-measure the pid, never reuse this one — the trap is named in the never-kill-by-a-remembered-pid law), then `bash scripts/start-lane-runner.sh`.** Until that happens this row is fixed on disk, not on the board. ⚠️ **THE ART HALF IS DELIBERATELY NOT CURED BY THIS, and F-1656-1 was right that the two want different cures.** For the ART slot `$wd` is `worktrees/art`, which is gitignored (`.gitignore:15`) and is **not** a git worktree — verified absent from `git worktree list`, which shows only `lane-a..d` under `worktrees/`. Its `.` pathspec is therefore ignored in full, so even a decoupled commit correctly stages **nothing**: that slot’s output is untracked **every batch** by design (F-1045-1), which is what the 538.22 MB AT RISK figure is made of. **That half still wants the salvage step made routine, and remains OPEN.** **GATE: the lane half closes when a restarted runner completes a task in a tree containing a gitignored path and the work arrives as a COMMIT — check `ahead` moved, not just that the files exist. The art half closes when a batch’s raws reach an object database without a fire remembering to salvage them.** — ORIGINAL ROW FOLLOWS, UNCHANGED — 🔵 **F-1656-1 (s1656 2026-08-11, FACTORY-OPS — NOT AN OWNER QUESTION. THE RUNNER FINISHED THE WORK AND THEN LOST IT.)** The `f1655-1` run of 12:01:07 ended `READY-FOR-GATES` with correct, complete output — and `lane/a` read **`ahead=0`**. `node scripts/lane-usable.mjs --all` reported the two files as **tracked dirt**, and `git status --short` showed them **`M ` in the first column: STAGED, never committed.** The run log’s final lines say why: the runner’s auto-commit `git add` was rejected — *"The following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files: `.wrangler`"* — so the add aborted, the commit never happened, and **110 lines of gated-quality work sat in a lane the next refill would `reset --hard`.** ⚠️ **THIS IS THE RESET MASSACRE PRECONDITION (Mistake #2) ARRIVING BY A NEW ROUTE, WHICH IS WHY IT IS WORTH A ROW RATHER THAN A FOOTNOTE.** w1-03 and polish-02 died because a lane was refilled over unmerged work. Every instrument the LANE-SAFETY LAW points at — `ahead`/`behind`, `main..branch`, `lane-freeze-classify`, and `lane-usable`’s own headline word — is derived from **commits**. A lane holding only *staged* work is `ahead=0` and answers **USABLE** to the safety question, which is the exact wrong answer. The standard pre-flight would then `reset --hard` and the work would be gone with no trace in any reflog anyone thinks to check. ✅ **Recovered here only because `lane-usable.mjs` reports TRACKED DIRT separately from untracked debris (the F-1299 lineage) and this fire read the WORD rather than the exit code** — `DIRTY` and `HOLDS` and `BUSY` all share `rc 2` deliberately. The content was committed **unchanged** as `b9f49748e` and drained normally at `cfc79bf29`. 📐 **The general shape, stated because it will recur under other filenames: a runner’s commit step that adds by any broad pattern can be aborted by a single gitignored path, and its failure is SILENT to every commit-derived probe.** `.wrangler` is a Cloudflare build artifact that appears whenever a deploy or `wrangler` invocation has run in that tree — so this is a property of the environment, not of this task. **OWED — not fixed here, deliberately:** the cure lives in `scripts/lane-runner-v3.sh`’s commit step (make the add path-scoped to the master’s TOUCH-ONLY list, or tolerate an ignored-path rejection and retry with the legitimate paths), which is **outside this slice’s firewall**, and the dispatch site is the coordinate §4.10b warns rots on every edit — so it needs its own corrective with the pointer re-base, not a drive-by. ⚖️ **A cheap partial mitigation worth considering in the same corrective:** have `lane-usable.mjs` say the word **STAGED** rather than folding staged content into generic `DIRTY`, since staged-but-uncommitted is the one dirt class that is finished work rather than someone’s scratch. 📈 **IT IS NOT A ONE-OFF — IT HIT TWICE IN ONE HOUR, IN TWO DIFFERENT SLOTS, AND I ONLY FOUND THE SECOND BECAUSE I DRAINED THE FIRST.** The ART run of 11:46:16 (`art-jumper-rotation-regen`) ends with the SAME rejection under a different ignored path: *"The following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files: `worktrees`"*. So `.wrangler` is incidental — **the defect is that the commit step adds a path set that may contain ANY ignored path, and one is enough to abort the whole add.** ⚠️ For the ART slot the consequence is worse and standing, because `worktrees/art/` is gitignored **by design** (F-1045-1): that slot’s commit can never succeed, so its output is untracked **every single batch** — which is exactly what the 538.22 MB / 588-file AT RISK figure in `scripts/art-staging-audit.mjs` is made of. Today’s 6 raw files (10.33 MB) were salvaged to `save/art-staging-20260811` (`d84a3706e`, pushed to origin). 💡 The lane case and the art ca