till seen `AT RISK 582`, and had to choose between disbelieving the instrument and disbelieving itself. **A cure that reports success while curing nothing is worse than no cure**, because it converts an open duty into a discharged one. ✅ **CURED `c5d077cec`:** the script now enumerates the staging roots and walks them recursively (F-1120-2's own shape, deliberately not a wider hardcoded path), and selects on the ONE property that defines the exposure — the blob is in no object database. **EVIDENCE = CROSS-INSTRUMENT AGREEMENT, two independent code paths: the audit says `582 files / 527.89 MB`; the fixed script's `--dry-run` says `582 file(s), 527.89 MB` across the same `982 files / 4 areas`.** Also batched the hashing through `--stdin-paths` + `cat-file --batch-check` (one process, not 982) and made it print the areas it walked, so a future divergence from the audit's denominator is visible rather than silent. 🔒 **GUARDED by `scripts/salvage-art-staging-reach.test.mjs` (8/8, 5.6s, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`) — and its RED PATHS ARE PROVEN BY MANUFACTURING BOTH HISTORICAL DEFECTS on scratch repos, because a passing guard never executes its own violation path:** the s1045 one-dir non-recursive reader finds **0** of the nested fixture, and name-based selection finds **0** of the regenerated-bytes fixture, while the real script clears both. The mutations assert they actually applied, so a future edit that makes one inapplicable fails LOUDLY rather than silently skipping. ⛔ **I DID NOT SALVAGE. The 530 MB repo-size decision is owner-gated (F-1640-1, F-1103-2) and that gate is UNCHANGED — this fire only made the option it offers executable.** ⓘ **A FIFTH INSTANCE OF THE VACUOUS-PRE-COMMIT-GREEN SHAPE:** `gate-caller-audit` PASSed before the commit and named nothing (its subject set is TRACKED files), then went **NO CALLER rc=1** on the post-commit run — grandfathered with a written reason, as its siblings are. That is the FOURTH recorded instance after `desk-carryforward-guard.mjs` (s1533), `desk-state-audit.mjs` (s1566) and `review-evidence-audit.mjs` (s1576); **four in 125 fires is no longer an anecdote, and the run-it-after-the-commit step is the only thing that has ever caught it.** 💡 **THE LESSON, and it generalises past art: when a defect is cured in an INSTRUMENT, ask the same question of every sibling that acts on its verdict. The audit was fixed three times by three careful fires, and not one of them asked whether the thing the audit TELLS YOU TO RUN had kept up.** A remedy text is a citation like any other, and citations rot — [[verify-the-target-surface-of-a-prescribed-cure]].
